/// # The sexpr Plugin {#sexpr}
///
/// @see mim::plug::sexpr
///
/// [TOC]
///
/// A backend that emits the program as symbolic expression, e.g. for equality saturation with [egg](https://egraphs-good.github.io/) or [slotted-egraphs](https://github.com/memoryleak47/slotted-egraphs).
/// Loading this plugin (`mim foo.mim -p sexpr`) appends an emission phase to the compilation pipeline that writes the fully lowered program to `<world>.sexpr` (or `a.sexpr` if the world is unnamed).
/// The output path can be overridden via `-X sexpr:o=<file>`; `-X sexpr:slotted` and `-X sexpr:types` select the format.
///
/// ## Dependencies
///
plugin opt;
import compile;
///
/// ## Phases
///
/// ### emit
///
/// Emits the symbolic expression of the current world.
/// This phase is spliced into the default pipeline (see `opt`) whenever the `sexpr` plugin is loaded.
///
axm emit: compile.Phase;
